WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.175
Local does not automatically mean secure.

00:00:03.255 --> 00:00:19.656
A model server bound to the wrong network interface, an unauthenticated API, a shared desktop session, or an exposed web interface can make sensitive prompts and compute available to unauthorized users.

00:00:19.736 --> 00:00:29.789
Apply least privilege, individual accounts, authentication, network segmentation, secure remote access, request limits, and administrative logging according to risk.

00:00:29.869 --> 00:00:35.689
Do not expose a local inference service directly to untrusted networks.

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:39.472
Handle model downloads as supply-chain inputs.

00:00:39.552 --> 00:00:53.308
Use trusted sources, review licenses and provenance, validate expected files where appropriate, scan supporting code, and avoid running unknown installers or model-specific scripts without review.

00:00:53.388 --> 00:01:01.325
Prompts, retrieved documents, outputs, uploads, caches, chat histories, telemetry, and logs may contain sensitive data.

00:01:01.405 --> 00:01:05.637
Define collection, access, redaction, retention, backup, and deletion.

00:01:05.717 --> 00:01:10.479
Disable unnecessary logging rather than assuming it is harmless.

00:01:10.559 --> 00:01:18.495
Patch the operating system, drivers, runtimes, interfaces, libraries, and integration code through a tested process.

00:01:18.575 --> 00:01:25.983
Back up configuration, prompts or evaluation assets where required, access controls, and service documentation.

00:01:26.063 --> 00:01:32.412
Models themselves may be reproducible downloads, but local customizations may not be.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:39.899
Monitor availability, latency, memory errors, queue depth, temperature, disk, failed requests, and unauthorized use.

00:01:39.979 --> 00:01:53.735
Responsible operation also requires model evaluation, user guidance, escalation for harmful output, and a clear decision about when a cloud or human expert is more appropriate.
